# EchoInStone Project Rules

- Always use english in this project. For commit messages, docstrings, comments, documentation and etc.

## Python Environment
- Always use `poetry run` prefix when running Python commands, tests, or scripts
- Example: `poetry run python main.py ...` or `poetry run pytest`
- The project uses Poetry for dependency management
- For media/YouTube/transcription from agents: use global `echoinstone` CLI (not sandbox one-liners). See `docs/ai/echoinstone-cli.md` and `AGENTS.md`

## Git Commit Messages
- When asked to create a commit message, write it to `commit_message.txt` file in the project root
- Use conventional commit format (feat:, fix:, etc.)
- Include detailed description of changes, problem, solution, and testing results

## Code Style
- Follow existing code patterns in the project
- Use type hints where appropriate
- Add docstrings to new methods and classes

## Testing
- Run tests using: `poetry run pytest`
- Test files are located in `tests/` directory
- BDD tests use pytest-bdd and are in `features/` directory
- For test output use `results_test/` directory

## Configuration
- Public configuration goes in `EchoInStone/config.py`
- Private configuration (tokens, secrets) goes in `EchoInStone/config_private.py`
- Both files should have the same structure for consistency

## Audio Processing
- Audio files are processed through the AudioProcessingOrchestrator
- Results are saved in timestamped directories under `results/`
- Output formats: JSON and CSV transcriptions

